<h1>About Hellsinker</h1>
<hr>
<div class="paragraph"><p><span class="standout">Hellsinker</span> is a bullet hell shoot-em-up ("shmup") video game, which involves lots of shooting at enemies while dodging dense, complex barrages of bullets.</p>
<p>While shmups are plentiful nowadays and have been iterated upon, Hellsinker has had a long time's worth of praise and infamy.
It sets itself apart from others in the genre in many ways, with difficulty ironically NOT being one of those ways.
Rather, the complexity of its mechanics and how much the game injects its setting directly into the gameplay, while mechanically and artistically inclined,
is off-putting to those wanting to get on-boarded into the gameplay as soon as possible.
Many people have not managed to stick with the game just from the main menu and game UI, for that matter - and within Hellsinker, progress is very much a
personal growth, arguably moreso than in other games. It accepts few transferable skills, and the poetic chaos of the story leaves several layers to unravel at a time.</p>
<p>To put it into perspective, the playable characters in Hellsinker ("EXECUTORs") are very, <i>very</i> different from each other.
Functionally, each consists of a sizable moveset thanks to the game's 3-button system which employs button combinations and tap speeds to do different attacks.
Because of this, choosing a character is like picking and committing to a <b>fighting game</b> character. Newcomers <i>will</i> be stuck in between
learning the "system mechanics" of Hellsinker and learning all of the options, tactics and strategies specific to their chosen EXECUTOR.</p>
<p>Despite that, practice will result in mastery of both, slowly resulting in less mistakes, optimization, and - where the game truly shines - aggressive, confident play.
Trying to clear the game for the first time is a journey on its own that can take weeks, but once everything comes together, the game truly becomes as deep as the ocean.
Levels become much more dynamic and hectic, reacting to your progress, while scoring becomes the encouraged, obvious goal - completely opposite of the defensive play
that's required when starting out.</p>
<p>If you're able to be patient and look past the superficial roadblocks, you'll be able to experience a carefully crafted and incredibly rewarding video game experience
unlike anything that's out there.</p></div>